  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-09-01T08:38:45.863Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Using the popular marshmallow_PB squish setup, there are a couple of observations in unity 2022:\n\n \n\n1) the avatar finger colliders do not interact with squish bone collider, only the palm and preconfigured colliders.\n\n2) when collision occurs the bone does not collapse as far as on 2019 regardless of the squish amount set\n\nadditional information: I have a second physbone component targeting the root of the breast bones themselves for movement so the squishbone components are only for squish animation, the main issue seems to be the insufficient squish and collision\n\n--\n\nUpdate 20th September 2023\n\nBased on comment by Bunkerotter, I can confirm removing the animated property for enabling and disabling collision seems to have fixed it. For whatever reason unity 2022 has broken this functionality",
